<title>CANADA: Canadian Pacific sells Laidlaw stake.</title>
<headline>Canadian Pacific sells Laidlaw stake.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY, Alberta 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Pacific Ltd said on Monday it sold all its interest in transportation and waste-management firm Laidlaw Inc in a deal expected to bring in net proceeds of C$1 billion ($722 million).</p>
<p>The Calgary-based conglomerate said it sold nearly 56 million Laidlaw shares, which it will receive after a reclassification of class A and class B voting stock into common shares, expected near the end of July.</p>
<p>The new shares were to be sold in instalments by means of share purchase rights at C$18.85 ($13.61) each, CP said.</p>
</text>
